<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Virgin Lands campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1954–1960s</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Virgin Lands campaign was a Soviet programme launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikita-khrushchev">Nikita Khrushchev</a> in 1954 to ease grain shortages by ploughing up unused steppe, mainly in northern Kazakhstan and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>. Hundreds of thousands of volunteers, many of them Russians and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukrainians">Ukrainians</a>, settled on new state farms. Harvests rose at first but fell with drought and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soil-erosion">soil erosion</a> in the early 1960s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/virgin-lands-campaign.jpg" alt="Virgin Lands campaign" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Post of the Soviet Union, designer G. Komlev / Почта СССР, художник Г. Комлев · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:25th_anniversary_of_conquering_virgin_land._USSR_block._1979.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
